= Collections and Publishing

Turn your notes into structured databases and into finished, professional outputs (spreadsheets, PDFs, books, and web pages).

Collections let you: 
- query and tabulate your notes like a database; 
- create publication project workspaces 

The publishing tools take one note or an entire collection and produce something that you can hand in, submit, or put on the web.
\

== In this section

- #wikilink("2 - Collections"). How collections turn your notes into a queryable, spreadsheet-like database: membership, filters, the table and agenda views, and CSV export.
- #wikilink("3 - Exporting and Publishing"). How to turn notes into professional outputs: single-note PDF/HTML/Pandoc export, accessible PDF/A and PDF/UA, and merged collection (book) and static-site export.

#callout("tip", title: "For Typst users")[ Because every note is Typst, your exports inherit Typst's typesetting quality. You get real PDF/A and PDF/UA, genuine HTML, and full control through set and show rules and #wikilink("3 - Scaffolds, Templates, and Packages"). ]
